WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.313
There are four basic relational terms that

00:00:02.339 --> 00:00:04.839
are useful to translate into everyday language

00:00:06.587 --> 00:00:08.771
A relation is essentially a table about

00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:11.879
one subject or event type A tuple

00:00:11.905 --> 00:00:14.471
is one row in that table An

00:00:14.497 --> 00:00:16.576
attribute is a column that describes each

00:00:16.602 --> 00:00:19.905
row A domain describes the allowed type

00:00:19.931 --> 00:00:23.628
and rules for a value For example

00:00:23.825 --> 00:00:26.868
the patient table is the relation One

00:00:26.881 --> 00:00:29.789
patient is a tuple Birth date is

00:00:29.815 --> 00:00:33.157
an attribute The allowed type and constraints

00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:34.525
on birth date are part of its

00:00:34.552 --> 00:00:40.282
domain One important word is atomic Atomic

00:00:40.308 --> 00:00:43.519
does not mean physically small It means

00:00:43.545 --> 00:00:45.558
the database treats the field as one

00:00:45.584 --> 00:00:49.890
value If a column contains a comma-separated

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.758
list of service codes and each service

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:54.113
needs to be searched joined or validated

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.942
separately that list is not a good

00:00:55.969 --> 00:00:57.995
atomic design for the relational model
